body:
> Each heading following another heading lead in the outline must have a heading level that is less than, equal to, or 1 greater than lead's heading level.

@domenic &ndash; FWIW, when I recently read this for the first time, I read it correctly.  For example, H2 is a heading level that is less than H1.

It is, [quite apparently](https://github.com/w3c/wcag/discussions/2722#discussioncomment-3851626), tripping people up.  Because (presumably), for example, 1 is less than 2.  Probably it is _mostly_ an issue for translation, but I submit that the phrasing could easily trip native English speakers who are not of a technical bent.  I cannot think of easy fix.
